# RIPER workflow

Five phases, each with its own access mode and artifact.

## 1. Research (read-only)
Output: research-notes.md. Understand what exists now.

## 2. Innovate (read-only, optional)
Output: approaches.md. 2-3 viable approaches with trade-offs.

## 3. Plan (write to docs)
Output: [task]-plan.md. Measurable success criteria, sequential steps with verify checks, rollback plan. Approval gate before Execute.

## 4. Execute (full access)
Follow the plan. Verify each step. Document deviations.

## 5. Review (read-only)
Output: review.md. Verify success criteria, run tests, retrospective.

## Phase transitions

Each transition is deliberate. Don't start coding during Research. Don't research mid-Execution. Don't skip Review.

## When to use

- Architecture changes
- Multi-file refactors
- Auth, payments, data integrity work
- Migrations

## When NOT to use

- Typo fixes
- Single-file bug fixes with obvious cause
- Prototype exploration
